+
+# Design Guidelines
+
+Our design system follows a set of core principles that ensure consistency and quality across all our products.
+
+## Design Principles
+
+### 1. Clarity First
+- Clear visual hierarchy
+- Intuitive interactions
+- Consistent patterns
+
+### 2. Flexibility & Modularity
+- Components that work in various contexts
+- Customizable while maintaining consistency
+- Composable building blocks
+
+### 3. Performance & Accessibility
+- WCAG 2.1 compliance
+- Optimized for all devices
+- Fast loading and rendering
+
+## Design Tokens
+
+### Colors
+
+Our color system is built on a foundation of purposeful colors:
+
+- Primary: Used for main actions and emphasis
+- Secondary: Supporting interactive elements
+- Neutral: Text, backgrounds, and borders
+- Accent: Highlights and special states
+
+### Typography
+
+We use a type scale that ensures readability and hierarchy:
+
+- Headings: Inter (600, 700)
+- Body: Inter (400, 500)
+- Code: Mono
+
+### Spacing
+
+Our spacing system uses a consistent scale:
+
+- 4px (0.25rem) - Minimal spacing
+- 8px (0.5rem) - Tight spacing
+- 16px (1rem) - Base spacing
+- 24px (1.5rem) - Medium spacing
+- 32px (2rem) - Large spacing
+- 48px (3rem) - Extra large spacing
+
+## Best Practices
+
+1. **Consistency**
+   - Use established patterns
+   - Follow spacing guidelines
+   - Maintain visual hierarchy
+
+2. **Accessibility**
+   - Ensure sufficient color contrast
+   - Provide text alternatives
+   - Support keyboard navigation
+
+3. **Responsiveness**
+   - Design mobile-first
+   - Use flexible layouts
+   - Test across devices
